## Blender, 7: a 512 x 512 matrix product as a 3D construct, a
## fly-through, arrays to video. A on the left wall, B on the ceiling,
## C on the front wall, every item a cell colored by its value; the
## camera starts far out (the whole cube: 134 million multiply-adds),
## flies to one work-group's 16 by 16 tile, then one work-item -- a row
## of A times a column of B, 512 products added into one item of C --
## and back out while C fills in, a work-group at a time. The product is
## X_eTaL-gpu's Accel ac:m_atmul; every place, color and time is an
## array worked out in X_eTaL (demos/MatmulFly.xtl); Video.xtl writes
## them into the script Blender runs. Explained in
## docs/literate/matmul.org.
## Run: just demo blender matmul-fly   (several minutes: 541 frames)

"bl:" u_se< "Blender"
"bp:" u_se< "Bpy"
"vd:" u_se< "Video"
"mf:" u_se< "MatmulFly"

# five stills (the document's pictures), then every frame as the video
script := ((1920, 1080, 512) mf:s_cene 0) c_at ((1.0 6.0 8.5 11.5 16.5, "matmul-fly") vd:s_tills 0) c_at (vd:r_ender "matmul-fly.mp4") c_at vd:report
n := "work/explain/run.py" bl:w_rite! bp:launcher
n := "work/explain/matmul-fly.py" bl:w_rite! script
"rendering five stills and 18 seconds (541 frames) with Blender (EEVEE) ..."
r := "work/explain/run.py" bl:r_un! "work/explain/matmul-fly.py work/explain/out"
"the run, and the error lines in Blender's log:"
lines := (n_ot r = f_irst "\n") p_artition r
d_isclose 1 s_elect lines
d_isclose 2 s_elect lines
"what Blender made:"
bl:r_ead "work/explain/out/report.txt"
